    },
    "excluded_steps": [],
    "format_errors": [],
    "steps": [
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 141,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 143,
        "char_start": 0,
        "effective_step": 1,
        "end_token_index": 49,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 50,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Recognize that for any \\(x\\) in the domain of \\(f(x)\\), \\(\\arccos x\\) and \\(\\arcsin x\\) are defined and their sum is \\(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 304,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 306,
        "char_start": 145,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 119,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 120,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Use the identity \\(\\arccos x + \\arcsin x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) to express \\(\\arccos x\\) in terms of \\(\\arcsin x\\): \\(\\arccos x = \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\arcsin x\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 464,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 465,
        "char_start": 308,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 187,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 188,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Substitute \\(\\arccos x = \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\arcsin x\\) into the function \\(f(x)\\):\n\\[f(x) = \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\arcsin x\\right)^2 + (\\arcsin x)^2.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 587,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 588,
        "char_start": 467,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 239,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 240,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Expand the squared term:\n\\[f(x) = \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)^2 - \\pi \\arcsin x + (\\arcsin x)^2 + (\\arcsin x)^2.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 690,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 691,
        "char_start": 590,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 284,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 285,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Combine like terms:\n\\[f(x) = \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)^2 - \\pi \\arcsin x + 2(\\arcsin x)^2.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 937,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 938,
        "char_start": 693,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 388,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 389,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Let \\(y = \\arcsin x\\). Since \\(\\arcsin x\\) ranges from \\(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) to \\(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\), \\(y\\) also ranges from \\(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) to \\(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\). The function becomes:\n\\[f(y) = \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)^2 - \\pi y + 2y^2.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1116,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1118,
        "char_start": 940,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 446,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 447,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: Identify the quadratic function \\(f(y) = 2y^2 - \\pi y + \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)^2\\). This is a parabola opening upwards (since the coefficient of \\(y^2\\) is positive)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1341,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1342,
        "char_start": 1120,
        "effective_step": 8,
        "end_token_index": 529,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 530,
        "step_number": 8,
        "text": "Step 8: Find the vertex of the parabola to determine its minimum value. The vertex form for a parabola \\(ay^2 + by + c\\) has its vertex at \\(y = -\\frac{b}{2a}\\). Here, \\(a = 2\\) and \\(b = -\\pi\\), so:\n\\[y = \\frac{\\pi}{4}.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1643,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1644,
        "char_start": 1344,
        "effective_step": 9,
        "end_token_index": 657,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 658,
        "step_number": 9,
        "text": "Step 9: Substitute \\(y = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\) back into the function to find the minimum value:\n\\[f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)^2 - \\pi \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)^2 = 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi^2}{16} - \\frac{\\pi^2}{4} + \\frac{\\pi^2}{4} = \\frac{\\pi^2}{8}.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2208,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2209,
        "char_start": 1646,
        "effective_step": 10,
        "end_token_index": 912,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 913,
        "step_number": 10,
        "text": "Step 10: Determine the maximum value of \\(f(y)\\) over the interval \\([- \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}]\\). Evaluate \\(f(y)\\) at the endpoints:\n\\[f\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = 2\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)^2 - \\pi \\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)^2 = 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi^2}{4} + \\frac{\\pi^2}{2} + \\frac{\\pi^2}{4} = \\frac{3\\pi^2}{2},\\]\n\\[f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = 2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)^2 - \\pi \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)^2 = 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi^2}{4} - \\frac{\\pi^2}{2} + \\frac{\\pi^2}{4} = \\frac{3\\pi^2}{2}.\\]"
      }
